README.v31_CMIP7
================

Purpose
-------
The same BSMYLE smbb ensemble as run.v21.LR.BSMYLEsmbb_CMIP7-05.sh, but with
E3SMv3.1 model code and CMIP7 forcing.

  Script : run.v31.LR.BSMYLEsmbb_CMIP7-05.sh
  Code   : /global/cfs/cdirs/mp9/e3sm_tags/E3SMv3.1   (maint-3.1, tag v3.1.0)
  Cases  : v31.LR.BSMYLEsmbb_CMIP7.<yyyy>-05.<mbr>
           under /pscratch/sd/n/$USER/v31.LR.BSMYLEsmbb_CMIP7/
  Build  : /pscratch/sd/n/$USER/v31.LR.BSMYLEsmbb_CMIP7/exeroot/build
           (member 001 builds; members 002-020 reuse e3sm.exe)

Same as the v2.1 CMIP7 script
-----------------------------
- Start 1990-05-01, 20 members, 28 months, hybrid start
- Initial conditions: v2.1 SMYLE ICs (v21.LR.SMYLE_IC.<yyyy>-05.01), including
  the pert.NN atmosphere perturbations for members 002-020
- Grid ne30pg2_EC30to60E2r2 (needed to use those ICs)
- Output streams (EAM fincl1-7, ELM h1, MOSART h1)
- Land surface files: surfdata_ne30np4.pg2_SSP3_RCP70_simyr2015_c220420.nc
  and the default v2.1 land-use timeseries (CMIP6 hist, 1850-2015)

What differs from v2.1
----------------------
1. Compset: 20TRSOI%CMIP7_EAM_ELM%SPBC_MPASSI_MPASO_MOSART_SGLC_SWAV
   - EAM%CMIP7 uses v3.1's built-in use case
     20TR_eam_CMIP7_chemUCI-Linoz-mam5-vbs: CMIP7 solar, GHG, oxidants,
     and all emissions (SO2 with 'stratvolc', SOAG0, NO, CO, VOCs, ...).
     No forcing overrides are set in user_nl_eam.
   - Volcanoes: v3.1 uses the CMIP7 stratvolc SO2 emissions and MAM5's
     stratospheric mode, with no prescribed volcanic aerosol. (The v2.1 script
     instead removes stratvolc and keeps the CMIP6 prescribed volcanic aerosol.)
   - Chemistry/aerosol: chemUCI + Linoz v3 + MAM5 + VBS SOA (v2.1: Linoz v2 +
     MAM4 + prescribed oxidants).
   - Land is ELM%SPBC (satellite phenology), as in v2.1, and NOT the
     ELM%CNPRDCTCBCTOP used by the standard WCYCL20TR-CMIP7 alias. The v2.1
     SMYLE land restarts are SP restarts with no carbon or nutrient pools, so
     prognostic BGC would start from zero vegetation and soil carbon.
2. Land use is CMIP6, not CMIP7. v3.1's CMIP7 land-use and surface data exist
   only on the r025 land grid (ne30pg2_r025_IcoswISC30E3r5). With these ICs
   the land runs on ne30np4.pg2, so the v2.1 files are set in user_nl_elm.
3. Machine environment: v3.1's pm-cpu config is mostly current, but for intel
   it does not pin cray-libsci, so it picks up the Perlmutter default
   (26.03.0 since the Nov 2026 update). That libsci_intel_mpi.so does not link
   with cray-mpich/9.0.1 (undefined MPI_Comm_f2c / MPI_Comm_c2f), and the MCT
   build fails with "configure: error: linking to Fortran libraries from C
   fails". After 'case.setup --reset' the script inserts
       <command name="load">cray-libsci/25.09.0</command><!-- intel pin -->
   after intel/2025.3 in env_mach_specific.xml (the version v3.1 already uses
   for gnu). Verified with a link test: 26.03.0 fails, 25.09.0 links.
   If you run 'case.setup --reset' by hand, re-apply this line.

Things to know before production
--------------------------------
- Atmosphere ICs: the v2.1 SMYLE eam.i files contain only meteorology
  (T, U, V, Q, PS, CLDLIQ, CLDICE, O3, ...). All chemUCI/MAM5 tracers (CO,
  NOx, VOCs, aerosols, E90, the Linoz *LNZ tracers) start from EAM defaults,
  as aerosols did in the v2.1 cases. Expect a chemistry/aerosol spin-up in
  the first months, and check that H2OLNZ/N2OLNZ/CH4LNZ (used in radiation)
  initialize sensibly.
- Cross-version restarts: EAM, ELM, MPAS-Ocean and MPAS-Seaice will read
  v2.1 restart/IC files with v3.1 code. Namelist generation accepts them,
  but compatibility at run time has NOT been tested. Run a short test first,
  for example run='S_1x5_ndays' with array=( 1 ).
- The standard v3.1 CMIP7 configuration (ne30pg2_r025_IcoswISC30E3r5, BGC
  land, CMIP7 land use) would need v3-grid initial conditions for every
  start date. None were found on mp9 or under inputdata/e3sm_init.

Checks done
-----------
- 'bash -n' passes.
- Scratch v3.1 case with this compset, grid, user_nl files and staged
  1990-05 v2.1 ICs: create_newcase, case.setup and preview_namelists
  succeed, and check_input_data reports no missing files.
  atm_in uses the CMIP7 solar, GHG, oxidant and CMIP7_2deg emission files.
  lnd_in uses use_cn=.false., the v2.1 ELM restart and the files above.
- Not yet done: build or run.

Case naming and biomass burning (updated 2026-11-25)
---------------------------------------------------
The CMIP7 cases are named *.BSMYLEsmbb_CMIP7.* and use SMOOTHED biomass-
burning (smbb) elevated emissions from
/global/cfs/cdirs/ccsm1/people/nanr/e3sm/inputdata/atm/cam/chem/trop_mozart_aero/emis/CMIP7_2deg-smoothed/
(11-yr same-month running mean of the BB sector, 1990-2023, the same method as
the CMIP6 smbb files; details in README.CMIP7_smbb there).
  v2.1: SO2 (nostratvolc), bc_a4, num_a1, num_a4, pom_a4, so4_a1 smoothed;
        SOAG stays the smoothed CMIP6 SSP370 file
  v3.1: SO2 (stratvolc), SOAG0, bc_a4, num_a1, num_a4, pom_a4, so4_a1 smoothed;
        NO2 aircraft, num_a2, so4_a2 = v3.1 CMIP7 defaults
Why smoothing was needed: in the E3SM CMIP7_2deg files the 1980-2014 BB is
identical to raw CMIP6 (max rel. diff ~1e-5), and median grid-cell interannual
variability jumps from ~9% (1980-1996) to ~95% (1997-2014). After smoothing:
9% -> ~15% (CMIP6 smbb: 9% -> 14%).
Between 2026-11-24 and 2026-11-25 the scripts were briefly named
*.BSMYLE_CMIP7.* and used UNSMOOTHED CMIP7 BB. Cases created before
2026-11-25 (e.g. v21.LR.BSMYLEsmbb_CMIP7.1991-05.*, which already ran) used
UNSMOOTHED CMIP7 BB despite the smbb name.
